=== Student Profile Ablation (analyze) ===

========================================================================
WINNER POPULATION CONFIGURATION
========================================================================

Overall rank #1: Single Canonical Student (B) (mode=single_canonical)
  learning_gain_mean=0.6411 (std=0.0610, CV=0.0952)
  seed_range=0.1514 (best seed 21, worst seed 42)
  success_rate_mean=0.3490
  adaptation_accuracy_mean=0.7864
  shannon_entropy=1.1523, actions_used_above_1%=4.2

Best mean learning gain: Single Canonical Student (B) (mean=0.6411)
Most stable (lowest LG std): Single Canonical Student (B) (std=0.0610, CV=0.0952)
Highest action diversity: Mixed Population (A) (entropy=1.2782)

--- Findings ---

1. Are student profiles a major source of DQN instability?
   YES. Heterogeneous profiles materially increase seed variance (mixed std=0.0929, single=0.0610, low-variance=0.1332). Different students reward different strategies, amplifying run-to-run spread.

2. Does a single canonical student improve stability?
   YES. Single canonical training cuts learning-gain std (0.0610 vs mixed 0.0929).

3. Does a single canonical student reduce generalization?
   YES. Single-student policies drop on mixed eval (same=0.6411, mixed=0.5920, gap=-0.0491). Lower training variance may reflect overfitting to one profile.

4. Best population design for the thesis:
   Single Canonical Student (B) - balances mean LG (0.6411), seed stability (std=0.0610), and action diversity (entropy=1.1523).
   Mixed students are HURTING stability; a canonical profile stabilizes training but verify mixed-population eval before claiming generalization.
